GHC 6.2.2 -- mhs: `f :: T = e` split into signature and binding
GHC accepted a type signature fused with its binding on one line
(`getBaseDir :: IO (Maybe String) = do return Nothing`) or a signature
directly followed by `= e` on the next line (HscMain initNameCache,
PrelInfo ghcPrimExports, TcRnMonad getBannedProcLevels). Haskell 98 does
not, and MicroHs rejects it; the binding gets its own left-hand side.

